      <title>Gemini 4 Hydrogen: Google's fast agentic model edges Argon on the Artificial Analysis index (51 to 50) at $1.50/$7.50 per million tokens</title>
      <link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-hydrogen/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-hydrogen/</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>AI &amp; Agents</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini-4-hydrogen__key-art__lockup__16-9.width-1300.jpg" alt="Gemini 4 Hydrogen key art" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>Flat pricing across a 1M-token context, 2.5x faster than 3.8 Flash with triple its Terminal-Bench score (57% vs 18.2%). New Orchestrator in Antigravity hot-swaps Carbon and Hydrogen mid-session: near-Carbon success rates at 24% less quota, 19% faster.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;Today, we're introducing Gemini 4 Hydrogen, bringing cutting-edge intelligence to everyone — with speed and efficiency for everyday coding and agentic workflows.&rdquo; - <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-hydrogen/">Koray Kavukcuoglu, Google DeepMind</a></blockquote>
