    <item>
      <title>Lurie breaks ground on a $72M Treasure Island behavioral health building: 300 treatment and recovery beds, opening late 2028</title>
      <link>https://www.sf.gov/news-mayor-lurie-breaks-ground-on-300-treatment-and-transitional-housing-beds-to-support-people-in-recovery</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.sf.gov/news-mayor-lurie-breaks-ground-on-300-treatment-and-transitional-housing-beds-to-support-people-in-recovery</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>44 new residential treatment beds, 84 new recovery-housing beds, and 172 beds relocating from old Navy housing. It's the first building in Treasure Island's stage-two development area, funded by Prop A bond money and state grants.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;In San Francisco, we are fundamentally transforming our behavioral health response by building a system that helps people earlier, creates more pathways into treatment and recovery, and delivers results for people and neighborhoods alike.&rdquo; - <a href="https://www.sf.gov/news-mayor-lurie-breaks-ground-on-300-treatment-and-transitional-housing-beds-to-support-people-in-recovery">Mayor Daniel Lurie</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.sf.gov/news-mayor-lurie-breaks-ground-on-300-treatment-and-transitional-housing-beds-to-support-people-in-recovery">SF.gov</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/13%3A%20loved%20%22Lurie%20breaks%20ground%20on%20a%20%2472M%20Treasure...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/13%3A%20meh%20on%20%22Lurie%20breaks%20ground%20on%20a%20%2472M%20Treasure...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/13%3A%20less%20like%20%22Lurie%20breaks%20ground%20on%20a%20%2472M%20Treasure...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//www.sf.gov/news-mayor-lurie-breaks-ground-on-300-treatment-and-transitional-housing-beds-to-support-people-in-recovery%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
